drm/vc4: display only: no V3D, no render node

Faraday's own change (docs/IMAGES.md §2), applied to the Pi's Compatible
build only (builds/compatible/buildroot.fragment). The Pi 3's vc4 driver
binds the GPU's 3D block, V3D, as one of its components and gives every
VC4 device a render node, /dev/dri/renderD128, which any process may
open. Faraday draws on the CPU into DRM's framebuffer emulation and needs
neither. This takes the V3D component out of the drivers vc4 registers,
so the block is never bound and its ioctls answer -ENODEV (they test
vc4->v3d), and drops DRIVER_RENDER, so no render node is created. The
display side (HVS, pixel valves, HDMI, DSI, the writeback) is untouched.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_drv.c
@@ -200,7 +200,6 @@
 	.driver_features = (DRIVER_MODESET |
 			    DRIVER_ATOMIC |
 			    DRIVER_GEM |
-			    DRIVER_RENDER |
 			    DRIVER_SYNCOBJ),
 	.open = vc4_open,
 	.postclose = vc4_close,
@@ -455,7 +454,6 @@
 	&vc4_txp_driver,
 	&vc4_crtc_driver,
 	&vc4_firmware_kms_driver,
-	&vc4_v3d_driver,
 };
 
 static int vc4_platform_drm_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
